  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 is the decisive Northwind win: the 5% figure is only a benchmark, so a model above it (Hearth 10 at 6.2%) can keep selling while corrective action proceeds, though exact per-model rates go to that model's customers. S5 mandates a recall above 8 per 100,000 with no interim period, which would reach Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, while the recall does not itself bar future sales. S3 (six-year retrofit) and S4 (36-month suppression start) also favour the companies with the lower installed-base and suppression-cost exposure, respectively. The S3 adoption-relative deadline could not be converted to months because the adoption date is not stated."
